  "source": {
    "rule": "Which Claude rows a surface reads, decided by the switch in claude-poll.json (on only when it reads version 1 and enabled true; missing, disabled and invalid are off) and by each row's provenance, never by the file it sits in. On: a Claude row counts only when its sourceKind is remote_api, from either file, the newest observation of an identity winning, plus the ACQUISITION availability row. Off: every Claude row except remote_api counts, with no weekly row and no ACQUISITION row. Other providers are never filtered. A Claude drift suppression is ignored; any other provider's suppression still applies. An availability flag on the ACQUISITION row never hides a reading. Each row takes rowDefaults for what it does not state; visible lists, by ref, exactly the rows the reader returns.",
